-- title:
--   Root property of the full-kernel quotient at every level
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number. The assertion is the predicate `FullKernelIsRootAt N`, which says the following. Write $H$ for the field of Hahn series with rational exponents and coefficients in an algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}$. For every Weierstrass curve $W$ over $H$ that is elliptic, every point $Q$ of the associated affine curve whose additive order is exactly $N$, and under the hypothesis $h\Delta$ that the discriminant of `W.fullKernelQuotient Q N` is nonzero — so that this curve is itself elliptic, the relevant instance being produced from $h\Delta$ — and for every datum `data : ModularCurve.ModularPolynomialData N`, consisting of a polynomial $\Phi \in \mathbb{Z}[X][Y]$ that is monic, of degree $\psi(N)$ (Dedekind's $\psi$) in $Y$, and satisfies $\Phi(j(q), j(q^N)) = 0$ as a $q$-expansion identity: the one-variable polynomial over $H$ obtained from $\Phi$ by applying to each coefficient the evaluation of integer polynomials at $j(W)$ has $j$ of `W.fullKernelQuotient Q N` as a root. Here `fullKernelQuotient` is the Vélu quotient formed from the sums $\sum G_x(P)$ and $\sum (x_P G_x(P) - y_P G_y(P))$ over the set `W.oddOrderSummingSet Q (N - 1)`.
--
--   This is the classical statement that the modular polynomial of level $N$ vanishes at the pair $(j(E), j(E/C))$ for $C$ the cyclic subgroup of order $N$ generated by a point, in the form needed over the Hahn-series field used for the Tate-curve analysis, with the quotient given by Vélu's explicit formulae for the full kernel. It is one of the hypotheses entering the level-$N$ dictionary between roots of the modular polynomial and cyclic subgroups of order $N$, and is used by [`ModularCurve.ModularPolynomialData.fibrePoly_j_eq_prod_fullKernelQuotient_j_of_transcendental_of_charZero`](thm.html#ModularCurve.ModularPolynomialData.fibrePoly_j_eq_prod_fullKernelQuotient_j_of_transcendental_of_charZero) and by [`ModularCurve.exists_elliptic_cycSub_orbitMap`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_elliptic_cycSub_orbitMap).
